Well, it was a decent try.  Here is a list of MHO of your mistakes and
better options:

> potions of full healing, scrolls of teleport, wands of teleport and
> digging, a set of useful tools, +2 Magicbane, a full set of useful
> spells (except Finger of Death). I spent a LONG time sacrificing to
> my god trying to get useful items - he gave me Magicbane and that
> was it. No spellbooks, other artifacts, no crowing from prayer,
zippo.

Well, that looks like you were doing something wrong.  A wizard should
have no problem praying for spellbooks, and should easily get  crowned
(+FoD).  You get spellbooks/crowned only by praying, not by
sacrificing, but sacrificing will let you pray more often, and praying
for spellbooks works only on an altar.

Methodology:
1) Complete the quest ("EoA for mana regen)
2) Camp by an altar.
3) Maximize luck
4) cast "create monster" (write the spellbook yourself if you need to)
5) Kill and sacrifice monster.
6) if message is not "a feeling of reconciliation" or "Your sacrifice
is consumed", goto 4
7) read spellbook if given
8) back to 4

You WILL get crowned and a lot of spellbooks this way.

> I did not know the Amulet of Yendor drained mana when casting spells.

You do now

> Then he steals the amulet (expected) and my artifact (also expected).

Letting the Wiz steal the "AoY is fine.  In fact, you can throw it to
him if he shows up and you can't insta-kill him.  But a Wizard should
never let Rodney take his quest artifact.
Put it in your bag the minute he shows up, but don't let him take it.
If he takes it, not only will he be immune to your magic attacks, but
it (the "EoA) can also be destroyed by black dragon breath.

Once Rodney has the amulet and you don't, you can now levelport without
him following you.  If you levelport up a single level, then descend
the stairs, you will now be able to fight him without his being able to
teleport away to heal.

The mana drain from the "AoY is not insurmountable.  Simple spells like
magic missile are still very effective, especially if you can bounce it
through him a couple of times.

> Trying to figure out some way to kill him more quickly, I hesitantly
> switched out to my quarterstaff

BIG mistake.  Two-handed weapons are a big risk, as you discovered.
Once you have killed Rodney, you will receive random cursings.  The
best way of resisting that is to always wield Magicbane.  If you want a
stronger physical attack, your best bet is a stack of +6 or +7 daggers.
Wizards can be expert in dagger, and you can throw a bunch of them
without letting go of Magicbane.  The only time I unwield Magicbane
after killing Rodney is if I need to wield a cockatrice corpse or egg,
or a potion of paralysis.

> I went to an altar, sacrificed repeatedly until I saw a clover leaf,
> then prayed. God displeased, no uncursing

You must have had negative luck. Most likely your luckstone had been
cursed as well.
Dropping the cursed luckstone, and sacrificing a few monsters before
praying would surely have worked.

Making holy water was not a workable idea.  You couldn't do a water
prayer unless you can pray successfully, and if you can do that then
you don't need holy water.
You could, however, have dipped the quarterstaff into the fountain.
That should have had a good chance of uncursing it.

Looking at your likely inventory, you probably had a wand of polymorph
and silver dragon scale mail.  You could have self-polymorphed into a
silver dragon or any monster without hands, which would have instantly
dropped the staff.  Remove your cloak first if you can, because dragon
polymorph will destroy your cloak and shirt.
And change back quickly, because you are much more vulnerable in
polymorphed form.

> Black light explodes. Beh, apply unicorn horn. Sicken, die.

Always check the status of your inventory after a "malignant aura".
Things like a cursed luckstone, unicorn horn, bag of holding, etc can
ruin your game.
Well, Die and Learn.

Better luck next time.

Happy Hacking.


